{
    "background_story": "Papito was a tiny, filter-feeding tunicate who lived in a vibrant coral reef. Despite his small size, he played a crucial role in the ecosystem, helping to keep the water clean by filtering out plankton and algae. Papito's transparent body glowed in the sunlight, and his delicate, sac-like shape allowed him to blend in with the surrounding sea fans and coral. As the reef's resident 'vacuum cleaner,' Papito took pride in his work, working tirelessly to keep his home pristine. At night, he would attach himself to a nearby rock, his siphons closed, and his body glowing softly in the dark waters. Papito's simple yet vital existence made him a beloved member of the reef community, and his tunicate friends looked up to him as a quiet hero.",
